  "id": "transfer-function-model",
  "term": "transfer function model",
  "definition": "A transfer function model is a time-series analysis approach used to estimate how changes in one measure over time are associated with changes in another measure over time, such as daily mobility patterns and search activity. In this source, it is used to study concurrent relationships between population movement indicators and mental health-, suicide-, and economic-stress-related searches.",
